# MoonCompiler fpc.cfg for Win64, rendered from scripts/fpc.cfg.win64.template
# (scripts/fpc.cfg.linux.template is the Linux twin).
#
# One template per target produces every fpc.cfg the drivers install: the
# product profile and the IDE profile.  build.ps1 and the stand script hand
# it to fpcmkcfg with -t and append the profile lines (the product ABI
# defines and the pinned memory manager, or the IDE define).
#
# The rule for this file: paths into the installed toolchain plus the parser
# switches every source in the repository has always been built with, and
# nothing else.  Optimisation, debug information, run-time checks, assembler,
# linker, target and the DEBUG/RELEASE defines are decided by the drivers,
# the Makefiles and the gates on the command line, never here.  The rendered
# file is checked line by line by qualification/build-driver/
# config_contract_gate.py, which also rejects every directive (#IFDEF,
# #IFNDEF, #ELSE, #ENDIF, #DEFINE, #UNDEF, #WRITE, #INCLUDE, #SECTION,
# #CFGDIR): a block that fires only under some define is exactly the silent
# switch this template exists to keep out.
#
# Left out of the stock FPC template on purpose: -O2 and -Xs under RELEASE,
# -gl and -Crtoi under DEBUG, -Xs whenever DEBUG is not defined, -ap,
# -Cp/-Op processor targets, -CX/-XX smart linking, the -XP cross prefix,
# the per-user fppkg unit path, the httpd unit path, the -FM unicode path,
# the toolchain lib path (nothing is shipped there) and the -l logo.
#
# %basepath% is the toolchain directory, which owns the installed units.

# Installed units: the RTL and the packages of this toolchain, in the stock
# FPC search order.
-Fu%basepath%/units/$fpctarget
-Fu%basepath%/units/$fpctarget/*
-Fu%basepath%/units/$fpctarget/rtl

# Tools shipped inside the toolchain (fpcres and the binutils).
-FD%basepath%/bin/$FPCTARGET

# Parser switches: g = goto and label, i = inline, c = C-style operators.
-Sgic

# Verbosity: errors plus info, warnings and notes.
-viwn
